Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-14-2000||04:53 PM||||After I recieved notification that I'm banned from Napster for downloading a Metallica song(along with over 300,000 other people) I decided I would try and find a way around it.  Supposedly, Napster does NOT log IP's, so I created a new email address and re-registered with different personal info.  Before I did this, I uninstalled Napster and also deleted the napster folder under programs files.  Afterwords, I used regedit to kill all refrences to Napster in the windows registry.  Then I downloaded the newest version of Napster.  I'm STILL banned!  How can this be happening if they don't long ip's?  Has anyone tried this yet?||||reg||9
